## Implementation summary (c004)
- Eliminates `torch.cat`; computes `processed_encoder = encoder @ W.T` and
  `processed_hidden = hidden @ W.T` as two weight-shared GEMMs. Split realized by writing two
  output tensors. `torch.no_grad`. Torch used only for shape/reshape-view/output-alloc/grid
  plumbing (no computational fallback of any kind).
- Single fused Triton kernel over a two-region M-grid (encoder tiles then image tiles); W
  (37.7 MB) kept hot in L2 across both regions; W read transposed via stride swap.
- fp32 accumulate/store; `tl.dot(..., input_precision="tf32x3")`.
- `@triton.autotune` over 14 tile configs keyed on (M_text, M_img); BK<=32 on the biggest tiles
  to keep fp32 SMEM within the H100 ~228KB/SM budget.

